television is great for telling  serialized stories over a long period of  time but not every TV series is meant to  last whether it's because of stiff  competition upheaval at the network or  simply being ahead of their time some  shows are canceled before they have a  chance to reach their full potential  none of these series made it past a  single season and we still aren't over  it  Clone High the animated MTV show clone  high followed clones of Abraham Lincoln  JFK Cleopatra and Gandhi among other  famous historical figures each  reinvented as a different teenage  archetype as they try to manage hormones  homework and a secret government program  with evil designs on their school she's  a user like [ __ ] you gir like a pair of  breasts the show's irreverent humor and  use of real-life historical figures were  bound to lead to controversy and its  depiction of Gandhi as a horny party  animal led hundreds of Indian citizens  to go on a hunger strike in protest  after the controversy the show was  ultimately cancelled with no hope of  renewal still while it ended too soon  for many fans the show's single season  remains a fascinating time capsule of  early 2000s MTV animation my so-called  life following Claire Danes character  Angela chase and her friends as they  dealt with real timely issues like  homophobia and abuse my so-called life's  depiction of teenage life was genuinely  groundbreaking from great dialog to well  written characters the show established  a unique depiction of a high-schooler  search for identity James's performance  was sometimes uncomfortably familiar and  the show's unflinching look at the less  discussed aspects of adolescence was a  critical hit he's bisexual  how can he be by anything he's a child  he's obviously very confused he's not  confused  he wears eyeliner unfortunately while  the show was beloved by its fans  James was ready to move on to new things  by the end of the first season and low  ratings meant the show was unlikely to  get a second season with or without her  still its influence reverberating  through nearly every high school set  series that followed Firefly  when discussing shows cancelled before  their time it's basically impossible to  exclude Firefly the show's focus on  science fiction adventures fused with  Western sensibilities combined with  creator Joss Whedon's trademark dialogue  made a huge impact on  those fans proved it with their now  legendary campaigns to save the series  which eventually resulted in a  big-budget movie continuation serenity  like any sci-fi series elements of  Firefly arguably haven't aged well but  it still remains a joy to see Zoe and  wash is one of the only functional  couples on the show there is traumatized  and cynical as the rest of the crew but  nonetheless refused to let their pass to  find them just one reason fireflies one  season voyage remains the focus of a  devoted fanbase the tick the original  live-action the tick followed the  addle-brained hero and his frustrated  former accountant turned super sidekick  Arthur using a mix of Seinfeld style  humor and off-brand Justice League type  antics to introduce a host of ridiculous  characters baby the madcap comedic  stylings and patrick warburton 'he's  booming voice have become almost  inseparable from the DNA of modern  comedies but the tick only lasted one  season while the show's run might have  been short it was definitely sweet with  a whole host of ridiculous allies and  enemies menacing our favorite bulging  blue bug evil never sleeps mr. Madoff  Quibbler although it's great that Amazon  resurrected the property without  Warburton and the rest of the original  cast on board the original takes  cancellation still feels like a missed  opportunity The Adventures of Brisco  County jr. starring the one and only  Bruce Campbell as Brisco The Adventures  of Brisco County jr. mixed classic  Western tropes like train robberies and  corrupt juries with anachronistic  technology like Rockets and projectors  much of the charm came from Campbell's  distinctive comic timing in every man  persona but the scripts were  surprisingly clever the show was set in  1893 a full 100 years before its airing  in 1993 which allowed for all sorts of  Futurama esque winking at popular  culture filtered through the lens of  classic genre trappings anyone who loves  Campbell's work or can simply appreciate  a perky good time needs to see this cult  classic the get-down Baz Luhrmann's the  get-down was always going to be subject  to scrutiny  Lerman is a love him or hate him  director and when you add in the massive  price tag and the difficult to define  genre the show is destined to leave some  of you are scratching their heads the  get-down tried to tell an unusual kind  of magical realist story about the  search for mythical wrecker  and passionate musical performances that  could convert foe to friends even when  the show approached abstraction its core  trio of kids in the slums of New York  brought an emotional reality that bed  rocked the series the way I see it all  of us here on this planet and we're on a  journey and it is a mystery  sadly the show just never found enough  of an audience but the entire run is  still part of the Netflix lineup just  waiting for the right viewers to get  hooked on its musical myth freaks and  geeks many shows have taken place in  highschool but none with the level of  uncomfortable frank honesty that fueled  freaks and geeks brought to viewers by a  flock of future famous faces and writers  including Judd Apatow Seth Rogen Linda  Cardellini Jason Segel and James Franco  it offered a unique depiction of  adolescence yeah well what are you gonna  do I don't know what are you gonna do  it's stunning to look back on the show  and see the on-screen evolution of some  of our favorite talent but even more  impressive is the timelessness of the  stories in the way they're delivered  although it was set in the early 80s  freaks 